    "updated_at": "2026-05-19T00:11:58Z",
    "body": "I am curious, actually, why there seems to be no \"proper\" way to set the path of a cannot-be-base URL? The pathname setter explicitly does nothing in that case.\n\nAs far as I know, nothing else in any URL is frozen like that. Except I guess not being able to change the specialness of a scheme but that's kinda a separate beast.\n\nWhile it makes sense that not all state overrides are valid, maybe this one should be?\n\nEdit: Btw, thank you for getting to my issues so quickly. Even if it's just triage it's nice to know at least someone's hearing me.",
